IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), PART VII.1, sections 152.07 (qualification requirements and
-- violations), 152.08 (qualifying period) and 152.09 (election between this Part and Part I).
-- Piece ei5, written by the piece agent ei5 (Sonnet 5.5). Layer 1: from the Act's text alone, no point of view.
--
-- The classes of violation are the keel's `Violation class`. What the Regulations decide is a plain input: the
-- amount of self-employed earnings fixed or determined by regulation for a qualifying period (reg 11.1, piece er1:
-- the $6,000 adjusted annually), the prescribed multipliers (none found), the interruption of earnings (reg 14.01,
-- piece er1), the average number of weeks of benefits (reg 13(2), piece er1), the election's manner (reg 25.1, piece er2).
-- This module imports no other ei5 module: the date a benefit period begins and the earnings of the qualifying
-- period are plain inputs the seat layer supplies from ei5-benefit-period and ei5-interpretation.
-- Dates: the section states fixed dates for the amounts of 2021 and 2022 (lines 2356-2357); no enactment or
-- commencement date.

§ `152.07 Qualifying for benefits`

§§ `152.07(1)(a) to (c) The first three requirements`

-- (a): at least 12 months have expired since the day on which the person entered into the agreement, or, if a period has
-- been prescribed for this section, a period at least as long as it. Twelve months expire on the same day of the month
-- twelve months later (`add months`, which clamps; fork F13). No period is prescribed in the Regulations as deposited;
-- reg 76.43 (piece er4) deems the condition satisfied in the interprovincial case, an input here.
-- src:2351 | (a) at least 12 months have expired since the day on which the person entered into an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1) with the Commission, or if a period has been prescribed for the purpose of this section, a period that is at least as long as that prescribed period has expired since that day;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(a) (src:2351)
GIVEN `the day on which the person entered into the agreement with the Commission` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the qualification is tested` IS A DATE
      `the period prescribed for this section, in months, if one is prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- out of range: s 152.07(1)(a); none found in the Regulations
      `the Regulations deem the condition satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 76.43 (piece er4)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.07(1)(a) at least 12 months have expired since the day on which the person entered into the agreement` IF
        `the Regulations deem the condition satisfied`
    OR  `add months` `the day on which the person entered into the agreement with the Commission` `the months required`
            AT MOST `the day on which the qualification is tested`
    WHERE
        `the months required` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the period prescribed for this section, in months, if one is prescribed`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 12
            WHEN JUST n THEN n

-- src:2352 | (b) the agreement has not been terminated or deemed to have been terminated;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(b) (src:2352)
GIVEN `the agreement has been terminated or is deemed to have been terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.07(1)(b) the agreement has not been terminated or deemed to have been terminated` IF
    NOT (`the agreement has been terminated or is deemed to have been terminated`)

-- src:2353 | (c) the person has had an interruption of earnings from self-employment; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(c) (src:2353)
GIVEN `the person has had an interruption of earnings from self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 14.01 (piece er1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.07(1)(c) the person has had an interruption of earnings from self-employment` IF
    `the person has had an interruption of earnings from self-employment`

§§ `152.07(1)(d) The amount of self-employed earnings required`

-- The dates that bound the two special amounts. Both ends of each period are counted ("beginning on ... and ending on").
-- src:2356 | (A) in the case where the person’s benefit period begins during the period beginning on January 3, 2021 and ending on September 25, 2021, and despite any amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, $5,000,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) (src:2356)
`s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) the first day of the period in which a benefit period must begin for the amount of $5,000` MEANS YearMonthDay 2021 1 3

-- src:2356 | (A) in the case where the person’s benefit period begins during the period beginning on January 3, 2021 and ending on September 25, 2021, and despite any amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, $5,000,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) (src:2356)
`s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) the last day of the period in which a benefit period must begin for the amount of $5,000` MEANS YearMonthDay 2021 9 25

-- src:2357 | (B) in the case where the person’s benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on September 24, 2022, and despite any amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, $5,289, or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(B) (src:2357)
`s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(B) the first day of the period in which a benefit period must begin for the amount of $5,289` MEANS YearMonthDay 2021 9 26

-- src:2357 | (B) in the case where the person’s benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on September 24, 2022, and despite any amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, $5,289, or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(B) (src:2357)
`s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(B) the last day of the period in which a benefit period must begin for the amount of $5,289` MEANS YearMonthDay 2022 9 24

-- Subparagraph (i): the person has not accumulated a violation in the 260 weeks before making the initial claim.
-- (A) a benefit period that begins from 3 January to 25 September 2021: $5,000, despite any amount fixed by regulation;
-- (B) a benefit period that begins from 26 September 2021 to 24 September 2022: $5,289, likewise;
-- (C) in any other case: $6,000 or the amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations, if any, for that
-- qualifying period (reg 11.1 adjusts the $6,000 each year; piece er1).
-- src:2355 | (i) if the person has not accumulated a violation in the 260 weeks before making their initial claim for benefits,
-- src:2356 | (A) in the case where the person’s benefit period begins during the period beginning on January 3, 2021 and ending on September 25, 2021, and despite any amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, $5,000,
-- src:2357 | (B) in the case where the person’s benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on September 24, 2022, and despite any amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, $5,289, or
-- src:2358 | (C) in any other case, $6,000 or the amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations, if any, for that qualifying period, or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(d)(i) (src:2355-2358)
GIVEN `the day on which the person's benefit period begins` IS A DATE
      `the amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- out of range: reg 11.1, s 152.33(c) (piece er1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.07(1)(d)(i) the amount of self-employed earnings required of a person who has not accumulated a violation` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day on which the person's benefit period begins` AT LEAST `s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) the first day of the period in which a benefit period must begin for the amount of $5,000`
           AND `the day on which the person's benefit period begins` AT MOST `s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) the last day of the period in which a benefit period must begin for the amount of $5,000`
            THEN 5000
        IF `the day on which the person's benefit period begins` AT LEAST `s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(B) the first day of the period in which a benefit period must begin for the amount of $5,289`
           AND `the day on which the person's benefit period begins` AT MOST `s 152.07(1)(d)(i)(B) the last day of the period in which a benefit period must begin for the amount of $5,289`
            THEN 5289
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, if any`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 6000
            WHEN JUST x THEN x

-- Subparagraph (ii): the person has accumulated a violation in the 260 weeks before making the initial claim: the
-- amount that would otherwise apply (that of subparagraph (i), for the date the benefit period begins) multiplied by
-- 1.25 (minor), 1.5 (serious), 1.75 (very serious) or 2 (subsequent), or the prescribed multiplier if one is prescribed.
-- src:2359 | (ii) if the person has accumulated a violation in the 260 weeks before making their initial claim for benefits, the amount referred to in this paragraph that would otherwise apply in respect of that self-employed person but for this subparagraph multiplied by,
-- src:2360 | (A) if the violation is a minor violation, 1.25 or the prescribed multiplier, if one has been prescribed,
-- src:2361 | (B) if the violation is a serious violation, 1.5 or the prescribed multiplier, if one has been prescribed,
-- src:2362 | (C) if the violation is a very serious violation, 1.75 or the prescribed multiplier, if one has been prescribed, or
-- src:2363 | (D) if the violation is a subsequent violation, 2 or the prescribed multiplier, if one has been prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(d)(ii) (src:2359-2363)
GIVEN `the class of the violation` IS A `Violation class`
      `the prescribed multiplier for that class, if one has been prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- out of range: s 152.07(1)(d)(ii); none found in the Regulations
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.07(1)(d)(ii) the multiplier for the class of the violation` IS
    CONSIDER `the prescribed multiplier for that class, if one has been prescribed`
    WHEN JUST m THEN m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the class of the violation`
        WHEN `a minor violation` THEN 1.25
        WHEN `a serious violation` THEN 1.5
        WHEN `a very serious violation` THEN 1.75
        WHEN `a subsequent violation` THEN 2

-- "has accumulated a violation in the 260 weeks before making their initial claim": the 260 weeks (1,820 days) that end
-- on the day before the claim is made (fork F14).
-- src:2355 | (i) if the person has not accumulated a violation in the 260 weeks before making their initial claim for benefits,
-- src:2359 | (ii) if the person has accumulated a violation in the 260 weeks before making their initial claim for benefits, the amount referred to in this paragraph that would otherwise apply in respect of that self-employed person but for this subparagraph multiplied by,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(d)(i) and (ii) (src:2355) (src:2359)
GIVEN `the day on which the violation was accumulated` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the initial claim is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.07(1)(d) a violation was accumulated in the 260 weeks before making the initial claim` IF
        `the day on which the violation was accumulated` AT LEAST `the day on which the initial claim is made` PLUS (0 MINUS (`weeks as days` 260))
    AND `the day on which the violation was accumulated` LESS THAN `the day on which the initial claim is made`

-- The whole of paragraph (d): the amount required, and whether the person had it. A violation in the 260 weeks is a
-- `Violation class`; NOTHING means none. When the person has several violations the text speaks of "the violation"
-- and says nothing of which counts (fork F16): the caller passes the one that applies.
-- src:2354 | (d) the person has had during their qualifying period an amount of self-employed earnings that is equal to or greater than the following amount:
-- src:2355 | (i) if the person has not accumulated a violation in the 260 weeks before making their initial claim for benefits,
-- src:2356 | (A) in the case where the person’s benefit period begins during the period beginning on January 3, 2021 and ending on September 25, 2021, and despite any amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, $5,000,
-- src:2357 | (B) in the case where the person’s benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on September 24, 2022, and despite any amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, $5,289, or
-- src:2358 | (C) in any other case, $6,000 or the amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations, if any, for that qualifying period, or
-- src:2359 | (ii) if the person has accumulated a violation in the 260 weeks before making their initial claim for benefits, the amount referred to in this paragraph that would otherwise apply in respect of that self-employed person but for this subparagraph multiplied by,
-- src:2360 | (A) if the violation is a minor violation, 1.25 or the prescribed multiplier, if one has been prescribed,
-- src:2361 | (B) if the violation is a serious violation, 1.5 or the prescribed multiplier, if one has been prescribed,
-- src:2362 | (C) if the violation is a very serious violation, 1.75 or the prescribed multiplier, if one has been prescribed, or
-- src:2363 | (D) if the violation is a subsequent violation, 2 or the prescribed multiplier, if one has been prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(d) (src:2354-2363)
GIVEN `the day on which the person's benefit period begins` IS A DATE
      `the amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the class of the violation accumulated in the 260 weeks before making the initial claim, if any` IS A MAYBE `Violation class`
      `the prescribed multiplier for that class, if one has been prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.07(1)(d) the amount of self-employed earnings the person must have had during their qualifying period` IS
    CONSIDER `the class of the violation accumulated in the 260 weeks before making the initial claim, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the amount under subparagraph (i)`
    WHEN JUST c THEN `the amount under subparagraph (i)` TIMES `s 152.07(1)(d)(ii) the multiplier for the class of the violation` c `the prescribed multiplier for that class, if one has been prescribed`
    WHERE
        `the amount under subparagraph (i)` MEANS
            `s 152.07(1)(d)(i) the amount of self-employed earnings required of a person who has not accumulated a violation`
                `the day on which the person's benefit period begins`
                `the amount fixed or determined in accordance with the regulations for that qualifying period, if any`

-- src:2354 | (d) the person has had during their qualifying period an amount of self-employed earnings that is equal to or greater than the following amount:
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1)(d) (src:2354)
GIVEN `the person's self-employed earnings during their qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount required` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.07(1)(d) the person has had during their qualifying period an amount of self-employed earnings equal to or greater than the amount required` IF
    `the person's self-employed earnings during their qualifying period` AT LEAST `the amount required`

-- The four requirements together.
-- src:2350 | 152.07 (1) A self-employed person qualifies for benefits if
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(1) (src:2350)
GIVEN `paragraph (a) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (c) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (d) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.07(1) a self-employed person qualifies for benefits` IF
        `paragraph (a) is met`
    AND `paragraph (b) is met`
    AND `paragraph (c) is met`
    AND `paragraph (d) is met`

§§ `152.07(2) to (7) Violations`

-- Subsection (2): the person accumulates a violation if the Commission issues a notice of violation to them in any of
-- three circumstances: penalties imposed under s 38 or s 41.1; guilty of offences under s 135 or 136; guilty of offences
-- under the Criminal Code relating to the application of the Act.
-- src:2365 | (2) A self-employed person accumulates a violation if in any of the following circumstances the Commission issues a notice of violation to the person:
-- src:2366 | (a) one or more penalties are imposed on the person under section 38, or under section 41.1 as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in section 38;
-- src:2367 | (b) the person is found guilty of one or more offences under section 135 or 136 as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in those sections; or
-- src:2368 | (c) the person is found guilty of one or more offences under the Criminal Code as a result of acts or omissions relating to the application of this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(2) (src:2365-2368)
GIVEN `the Commission issues a notice of violation to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more penalties are imposed on the person under section 38, or under section 41.1 as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in section 38` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: ss 38 and 41.1 (piece ei2)
      `the person is found guilty of one or more offences under section 135 or 136 as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in those sections` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: ss 135 and 136 (piece ei4)
      `the person is found guilty of one or more offences under the Criminal Code as a result of acts or omissions relating to the application of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the Criminal Code
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.07(2) a self-employed person accumulates a violation` IF
        `the Commission issues a notice of violation to the person`
    AND (   `one or more penalties are imposed on the person under section 38, or under section 41.1 as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in section 38`
         OR `the person is found guilty of one or more offences under section 135 or 136 as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in those sections`
         OR `the person is found guilty of one or more offences under the Criminal Code as a result of acts or omissions relating to the application of this Act`)

-- Subsection (4): the amount under (3)(b) cannot exceed the amount of benefits that could have been paid to the person if
-- they had not been disentitled or had met the qualification requirements.
-- src:2371 | (a) the amount of the overpayment of benefits under this Part resulting from the acts or omissions on which the violation is based, and
-- src:2372 | (b) if the self-employed person is disentitled from receiving benefits under this Part, or the act or omission on which the violation is based relates to qualification requirements under subsection (1), the amount determined, subject to subsection (4), by multiplying the self-employed person’s weekly rate of benefits by the average number of weeks of benefits under this Part, as determined under the regulations.
-- src:2373 | Maximum
-- src:2374 | (4) The maximum amount to be determined under paragraph (3)(b) is the amount of benefits that could have been paid to the self-employed person if they had not been disentitled or had met the qualification requirements under subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(3)(b) and (4) (src:2371-2374)
GIVEN `the person is disentitled from receiving benefits under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission relates to the qualification requirements under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's weekly rate of benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the average number of weeks of benefits under this Part, as determined under the regulations` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: reg 13(2) (piece er1)
      `the amount of benefits that could have been paid if the person had not been disentitled or had met the qualification requirements` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.07(3)(b) the weekly rate of benefits multiplied by the average number of weeks, held to the maximum of subsection (4)` IS
    IF `the person is disentitled from receiving benefits under this Part` OR `the act or omission relates to the qualification requirements under subsection (1)`
    THEN min (`the person's weekly rate of benefits` TIMES `the average number of weeks of benefits under this Part, as determined under the regulations`)
             `the amount of benefits that could have been paid if the person had not been disentitled or had met the qualification requirements`
    ELSE 0

-- Subsection (3): the value of a violation is the total of (a) the overpayment of benefits under this Part resulting from
-- the acts or omissions and (b) the amount just computed.
-- src:2370 | (3) The value of a violation is the total of
-- src:2371 | (a) the amount of the overpayment of benefits under this Part resulting from the acts or omissions on which the violation is based, and
-- src:2372 | (b) if the self-employed person is disentitled from receiving benefits under this Part, or the act or omission on which the violation is based relates to qualification requirements under subsection (1), the amount determined, subject to subsection (4), by multiplying the self-employed person’s weekly rate of benefits by the average number of weeks of benefits under this Part, as determined under the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(3) (src:2370-2372)
GIVEN `the amount of the overpayment of benefits under this Part resulting from the acts or omissions on which the violation is based` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount under paragraph (3)(b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.07(3) the value of a violation` IS
    `the amount of the overpayment of benefits under this Part resulting from the acts or omissions on which the violation is based` PLUS `the amount under paragraph (3)(b)`

-- Subsection (5): "Except for violations for which a warning was imposed", a violation is a minor, serious or very serious
-- violation by its value (less than $1,000; $1,000 or more but less than $5,000; $5,000 or more) and, under (b), a subsequent
-- violation if the notice of violation is issued within 260 weeks after the person accumulates another violation, "even if the
-- acts or omissions on which it is based occurred before". Paragraph (b) names a class of its own, so it governs when both
-- apply (fork F15). A violation for which a warning was imposed has no class: NOTHING. The keel's `Violation class` has
-- the same four classes.
-- src:2376 | (5) Except for violations for which a warning was imposed, each violation is classified as a minor, serious, very serious or subsequent violation as follows:
-- src:2377 | (a) if the value of the violation is
-- src:2378 | (i) less than $1,000, it is a minor violation,
-- src:2379 | (ii) $1,000 or more, but less than $5,000, it is a serious violation, or
-- src:2380 | (iii) $5,000 or more, it is a very serious violation; and
-- src:2381 | (b) if the notice of violation is issued within 260 weeks after the person accumulates another violation, it is a subsequent violation, even if the acts or omissions on which it is based occurred before the person accumulated the other violation.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(5) (src:2376-2381)
GIVEN `a warning was imposed for the violation` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 41.1 (piece ei2)
      `the value of the violation` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the notice of violation is issued` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person accumulated another violation, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Violation class`
DECIDE `s 152.07(5) the class of a violation` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a warning was imposed for the violation` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the notice is issued within 260 weeks after the person accumulates another violation` THEN JUST `a subsequent violation`
        IF `the value of the violation` LESS THAN 1000 THEN JUST `a minor violation`
        IF `the value of the violation` LESS THAN 5000 THEN JUST `a serious violation`
        OTHERWISE JUST `a very serious violation`
    WHERE
        `the notice is issued within 260 weeks after the person accumulates another violation` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the person accumulated another violation, if they did`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST other THEN
                    `the day on which the notice of violation is issued` AT LEAST other
                AND `the day on which the notice of violation is issued` AT MOST `the last day of` (`weeks as days` 260) `days after` other

-- Subsection (6): a violation accumulated under section 7.1 is deemed to be accumulated under this section on the day the
-- notice of violation was given.
-- src:2383 | (6) A violation accumulated by an individual under section 7.1 is deemed to be a violation accumulated by the individual under this section on the day on which the notice of violation was given to the individual.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(6) (src:2383)
GIVEN `the violation was accumulated by the individual under section 7.1` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 7.1 (piece ei1)
      `the day on which the notice of violation was given to the individual` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 152.07(6) the day on which a violation accumulated under section 7.1 is deemed to be accumulated under this section` IS
    IF `the violation was accumulated by the individual under section 7.1`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the notice of violation was given to the individual`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (7): a violation may not be taken into account under paragraph (1)(d) in more than two initial claims by the
-- individual if they qualified for benefits in each of those two claims. So it may be taken into account in this claim only
-- if it has been taken into account (and the individual qualified) in fewer than two earlier initial claims.
-- src:2385 | (7) A violation may not be taken into account under paragraph (1)(d) in more than two initial claims by an individual for benefits under this Act if the individual who accumulated the violation qualified for benefits in each of those two initial claims, taking into account subparagraph (1)(d)(ii), subsection 7.1(1) or regulations made under Part VIII, as the case may be.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.07(7) (src:2385)
GIVEN `the number of earlier initial claims in which the violation was taken into account and the individual qualified for benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.07(7) the violation may be taken into account under paragraph (1)(d) in this initial claim` IF
    `the number of earlier initial claims in which the violation was taken into account and the individual qualified for benefits` LESS THAN 2

§ `152.08 Qualifying period`

-- "The year immediately before the year during which their benefit period begins": the calendar year (s 2(1) "year").
-- src:2387 | 152.08 (1) The qualifying period of a self-employed person is the year immediately before the year during which their benefit period begins.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.08(1) (src:2387)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 152.08(1) the qualifying period of a self-employed person` IS
    `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay (`s 2(1) the year containing` `the day on which the benefit period begins` MINUS 1) 1 1),
                        (YearMonthDay (`s 2(1) the year containing` `the day on which the benefit period begins` MINUS 1) 12 31)

-- src:2389 | (2) A self-employed person’s self-employed earnings during a qualifying period may not be taken into account in respect of more than one initial claim for benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.08(2) (src:2389)
GIVEN `the number of other initial claims in respect of which the person's self-employed earnings during that qualifying period were taken into account` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.08(2) the self-employed earnings during a qualifying period may be taken into account` IF
    `the number of other initial claims in respect of which the person's self-employed earnings during that qualifying period were taken into account` EQUALS 0

§ `152.09 Benefits under this Part and Part I`

-- Subsection (1): a person who qualifies under this Part as a self-employed person and under Part I as an insured person may
-- receive benefits under one Part only and must, in the prescribed manner (reg 25.1: in writing, piece er2), at the time of
-- making an initial claim, elect under which Part. The result is the Part under which benefits are to be paid; NOTHING when
-- the person qualifies under both and has made no election, or elected a Part they do not qualify under, or qualifies under neither.
-- src:2391 | 152.09 (1) If an individual qualifies for benefits under this Part as a self-employed person and for benefits under Part I as an insured person, the individual may receive benefits under one Part only and, to do so, the individual must, in the prescribed manner, at the time of making an initial claim for benefits, elect under which Part benefits are to be paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.09(1) (src:2391)
GIVEN `the individual qualifies for benefits under this Part as a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual qualifies for benefits under Part I as an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Part elected in the prescribed manner at the time of making the initial claim, if any` IS A MAYBE `Part of the Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Part of the Act`
DECIDE `s 152.09(1) the Part under which benefits are to be paid` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the individual qualifies for benefits under this Part as a self-employed person` AND `the individual qualifies for benefits under Part I as an insured person`
            THEN CONSIDER `the Part elected in the prescribed manner at the time of making the initial claim, if any`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN JUST elected THEN
                     IF elected EQUALS `Part VII.1` OR elected EQUALS `Part I`
                     THEN JUST elected
                     ELSE NOTHING
        IF `the individual qualifies for benefits under this Part as a self-employed person` THEN JUST `Part VII.1`
        IF `the individual qualifies for benefits under Part I as an insured person` THEN JUST `Part I`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2391 | 152.09 (1) If an individual qualifies for benefits under this Part as a self-employed person and for benefits under Part I as an insured person, the individual may receive benefits under one Part only and, to do so, the individual must, in the prescribed manner, at the time of making an initial claim for benefits, elect under which Part benefits are to be paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.09(1) (src:2391)
GIVEN `the individual qualifies for benefits under this Part as a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual qualifies for benefits under Part I as an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.09(1) the individual must elect the Part under which benefits are to be paid` IF
        `the individual qualifies for benefits under this Part as a self-employed person`
    AND `the individual qualifies for benefits under Part I as an insured person`

-- Subsection (2): the election binds the individual, in respect of the initial claim, for all benefits payable during the
-- benefit period for any of the six special reasons (a) to (f); it says nothing of regular benefits, which Part VII.1
-- does not pay.
-- src:2393 | (2) The election is binding on the individual in respect of the initial claim for all benefits payable, for any of the following reasons, during the benefit period established in relation to the initial claim:
-- src:2394 | (a) pregnancy;
-- src:2395 | (b) caring for one or more new-born children of the self-employed person, or one or more children placed with the self-employed person for the purpose of adoption;
-- src:2396 | (c) a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine;
-- src:2397 | (d) providing care or support to one or more family members;
-- src:2398 | (e) providing care or support to one or more critically ill children; and
-- src:2399 | (f) providing care or support to one or more critically ill adults.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.09(2) (src:2393-2399)
GIVEN reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.09(2) the election is binding in respect of the reason` IF
    `s 2(1) special benefits` reason
